  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-ui-filter (npm)",
  "details": "On require, this package (a \"UI toolkit\") fingerprints the OS/architecture and downloads a platform-specific binary from three Cloudflare Workers hosts (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe, with a DNS-TXT chunked-transfer fallback from c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The fetched binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process via cmd.exe /c start /b or /bin/sh -c \"fp \u0026\". The package executes this remote binary download-and-run automatically on import, with no user interaction.",
